## 🚨 Strict Regional Routing & Authentication Rules

### 1. EU Environment
- **Web UI:** `https://app.datadoghq.com/`
- **Access Protocol:** Connected **Datadog MCP Server**.
- Query logs and traces using the registered Datadog MCP tools.

### 2. US Environment (GovCloud / ddog-gov.com)
- **Web UI:** `https://app.ddog-gov.com/`
- **API Base URL:** `https://api.ddog-gov.com/`
- **Authentication Method:** **Bearer Token ONLY**.
  - **CRITICAL**: We do **NOT** use `apiKey` or `appKey` for US Datadog.
  - Read `datadog.us.accessToken` from `shaagent.config.json`.
  - Pass this token strictly in the HTTP header:
    ```http
    Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
    ```
  - Any request attempting to use `DD-API-KEY` or `DD-APPLICATION-KEY` headers will fail. **Always use Bearer token authorization.**

---

## US Datadog API Request Specifications

When querying the US Datadog environment (`https://api.ddog-gov.com`), use the following exact API requests:

### 1. Log Search API Request
Search log events matching the correlation ID in the incident time window:

```bash
curl -X POST "https://api.ddog-gov.com/api/v2/logs/events/search" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${DD_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "filter": {
      "query": "@correlationId:\"'"${CORRELATION_ID}"'\" OR @trace_id:\"'"${CORRELATION_ID}"'\" OR \"'"${CORRELATION_ID}"'\"",
      "from": "'"${START_TIME_ISO}"'",
      "to": "'"${END_TIME_ISO}"'"
    },
    "sort": "-timestamp",
    "page": {
      "limit": 50
    }
  }'
```

#### Parsing Log Response:
- Iterate through `data[]` entries.
- Extract:
  - `attributes.service`: Failing microservice name
  - `attributes.status`: Log level (`error`, `critical`, `warn`)
  - `attributes.message`: Raw log text
  - `attributes.attributes.error.stack` or `attributes.attributes.exception`: Full stack trace
  - `attributes.attributes.error.message` or `attributes.attributes.error.kind`: Error type

---

### 2. APM / Span Search API Request
Retrieve trace spans matching the correlation ID to pinpoint the failing service and span:

```bash
curl -X POST "https://api.ddog-gov.com/api/v2/spans/events/search" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${DD_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "data": {
      "type": "spans_search_request",
      "attributes": {
        "filter": {
          "query": "@correlationId:\"'"${CORRELATION_ID}"'\" OR @trace_id:\"'"${CORRELATION_ID}"'\" OR \"'"${CORRELATION_ID}"'\"",
          "from": "'"${START_TIME_ISO}"'",
          "to": "'"${END_TIME_ISO}"'"
        },
        "sort": "-timestamp",
        "page": {
          "limit": 25
        }
      }
    }
  }'
```

#### Parsing APM Response:
- Look for spans with `attributes.attributes.error: 1`.
- Extract:
  - `attributes.attributes.resource_name`: HTTP route / DB query / method name
  - `attributes.attributes.service_name`: Emitting service
  - `attributes.attributes.error.type`: Exception class (e.g. `System.NullReferenceException`, `java.lang.IllegalArgumentException`)
  - `attributes.attributes.error.msg`: Exception message
  - `attributes.attributes.error.stack`: Error stack trace

